# Real device-location data - only Configuration.example.json (placeholder template) is
# tracked. Written by /api/save-config (Start-WebServer.ps1). Configuration.json is the
# -NoEncryption-mode plaintext equivalent - same sensitivity, ignored for the same reason.
PS_NetworkMapper/Configuration.json.enc
PS_NetworkMapper/Configuration.json

# Scraper output - contains real internal topology/IP data, not fixtures. Every real crawl
# writes into the Network_Maps/ folder (see Start-NetworkMapper.ps1's $SnapshotDir), named
# NetworkMap_<timestamp>.json(.enc) or ...tmp... while a write is in progress. The two
# shipped sample snapshots happen to follow that same naming convention on purpose (so
# "Load Folder of Snapshots" can load them together to demo the multi-snapshot/diff
# features) - the explicit `!` exceptions below are the only tracked files matching the
# pattern; any OTHER NetworkMap_*.json(.enc) is real crawl output and stays ignored.
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_*.json
PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_*.json.enc
!PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_2026-08-13_091500.json
!PS_NetworkMapper/Network_Maps/NetworkMap_2026-08-20_143207.json
PS_NetworkMapper/Mapper_Debug.log
PS_NetworkMapper/RawDumps/

# Local git worktrees used for isolated feature-plan execution (superpowers:using-git-worktrees).
.worktrees/

# Claude Code working directory: per-session audit notes and runtime state, not source.
.claude/

# Raw switch session captures used as parsing ground truth while debugging. Real device
# output (hostnames, IPs, MACs), same sensitivity as Network_Maps/ above.
PS_NetworkMapper/Raw_*.txt

# Atomic-write temps from lib/FileHelpers.ps1 (<dest>.<pid>.<guid>.tmp). A crash between the
# write and the rename leaves one behind, and under -NoEncryption the Configuration.json temp
# is plaintext SSH credentials - the exact-name rule above does not match it.
PS_NetworkMapper/**/*.tmp

# Runtime debug logs. Mapper_Debug.log is covered by name above, but WebServer.ps1 writes
# Network_Maps/ScanNetwork_Debug.log on every browser-triggered scan.
PS_NetworkMapper/**/*.log

# Get-JunosNodeData.ps1 derives RawDumps/ from the debug-log directory, so it does not always
# land at PS_NetworkMapper/RawDumps/. Unanchored to cover Network_Maps/RawDumps/ too.
PS_NetworkMapper/**/RawDumps/

# Protect-MapperFile.ps1's derived decrypt output - plaintext credentials.
PS_NetworkMapper/**/*.decrypted.json
